724 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Backend Developer \174 Feb 2024 \055 Mar 2024 \nSimplified Practice\n\nDevelopment of a recipe website project utilizing the YouTube API and tools such as PHP\054 Laravel\054 and Sanctum for cookie based authentication\054 role management\054 and cloud hosting\073 the project includes video playback and comments for each video\054 along with the implementation of client\055side logic\056\n\nBackend Developer \174 Mar 2024 \055 Abr 2024 \nMoa Travel\n\nUnder the guidance of a senior developer\054 I worked on a monolithic project using Python \050FastAPI\051\054 SQL \050PostgreSQL\051\054 and Docker\054 handling the implementation of controllers\054 routes\054 and cloud services such as AWS S3 to support the business logic of a travel company\056\n\n\nBackend Developer \174 Jun 2024 \055 Dic 2024 \nNextStation Chile\n\nResponsible for managing various components of microservices\055based projects built with Python\057FastAPI\054 SQLAlchemy\054 PostgreSQL\054 and Docker\054 I developed controllers\054 routes\054 and services to handle business logic for a solar panel company and a church management API\054 integrating Apple and Google login via Firebase\n\nSoftware Developer \174 Marzo 2025 \055 sept 2025\nLeadgrowth\n\nI handled the development\054 planning\054 and integration of various services across different platforms specifically GoHighLevel utilizing tools such as EC2\054 S3 buckets\054 Hostinger\054 and Nginx for hosting\056 I used Docker for the VPS where the created APIs were deployed\056 Regarding the codebase\054 I used Python as the primary language with FastAPI as the main framework\054 and employed PostgreSQL and MySQL for databases\056 For architecture\054 I primarily utilized monolithic and hexagonal patterns\054 optimizing client and data flows and increasing productivity by 80\045 based on the data obtained\073 for certain workflows\054 I implemented n8n for automation\054 integrating the ChatGPT API and DeepSeek R8\056\n\n\nSoftware Developer \174 sept 2025 \nFreelance\n\nI was part of a cross\055functional team responsible for developing an AI\055powered platform for intelligent product processing\056 The team operated under an Agile model\054 utilizing continuous integration and automated deployment\056\015\nI collaborated on integrating language models \050OpenAI API\054 Gemini\051 into the product processing workflow\054 using OpenAI Batch for high volume asynchronous tasks\056 The team defined the prompts and the validation logic for the AI\055generated results\056\015\nI participated in designing and deploying services using AWS Lambda\054 EC2\054 ECS\054 ECR\054 API Gateway\054 Cognito\054 S3\054 and CloudWatch\056 This enabled the team to automatically scale based on product pipeline demand\056\015\nWorking with the data team\054 I implemented a workflow where raw product data was transformed using RAG \050Retrieval\055Augmented Generation\051\056 Each stage of the pipeline validated that the AI \013\013processed the information correctly and generated results aligned with business requirements\056\015\nI also participated in backend development using Python and FastAPI and collaborated closely with the frontend team working with React and TypeScript\057JavaScript to visualize pipeline results\056\015\nI assisted in managing MongoDB to store pipeline states\054 facilitating auditing and failure retries\054 and helped configure GitHub Actions to automate testing\054 builds\054 and deployments\054 thereby reducing manual errors and accelerating team delivery\056\n\n)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 725 0 R
     /Pg 716 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

